          %h2#literature Literature
          %blockquote
            %p
              The following references concern the classical part of the subject. For the references connecting Hausdorff series to
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Drinfeld+associators"} Drinfeld associators
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck-Teichmueller+group"} Grothendieck-Teichmueller group
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kashiwara-Vergne+conjecture"} Kashiwara-Vergne conjecture
              see there.
          %p Early discussion:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Rüdiger Achilles, Andrea Bonfiglioli:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The early proofs of the theorem of Campbell, Baker, Hausdorff, and Dynkin
                %strong 66
                (2012) 295–358 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00407-012-0095-8"}> doi:10.1007/s00407-012-0095-8
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eugene+B.+Dynkin"}> Eugene B. Dynkin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Calculation of the coefficents in the Campbell-Hausdorff formula
                %strong 57
                (1947) 323-326
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wilhelm+Magnus"}> Wilhelm Magnus
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A connection between the Baker-Hausdorff formula and a problem of Burnside
                %strong 52
                (1950) 111-126
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kuo-Tsai+Chen"}> Kuo-Tsai Chen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Integration of paths, geometric invariants and a generalized Baker–Hausdorff formula
                = succeed ":1" do
                  %strong 65
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2307/1969671"} doi
                %a{:href => "http://www.jstor.org/stable/1969671"} jstor
          %p
            Most monographs on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebras"} Lie algebras
            discuss the Hausdorff series, for instance:
          %ul
            %li#Serre64
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Pierre+Serre"}> Jean-Pierre Serre
                , Section IV.7 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lie Algebras and Lie Groups – 1964 Lectures given at Harvard University
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 1500
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-540-70634-2"} doi:10.1007/978-3-540-70634-2
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicolas+Bourbaki"}> Nicolas Bourbaki
                , Chapter 2 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lie groups and Lie algebras
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/9783540642428"} ISBN:9783540642428
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gerhard+P.+Hochschild"}> Gerhard P. Hochschild
                , p. 226 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Basic theory of algebraic groups and Lie algebras
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 75
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4613-8114-3_16"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4613-8114-3_16
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M.+M.+Postnikov"}> M. M. Postnikov
                ,
                %em Lectures on geometry: Semester V, Lie groups and algebras
                (1986) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://archive.org/details/postnikov-lectures-in-geometry-semester-v-lie-group-and-lie-algebras"}> ark:/13960/t4cp9jn4p
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hans+Duistermaat"}> Hans Duistermaat
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Johan+A.+C.+Kolk"} Johan A. C. Kolk
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Dynkin’s formula
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lie groups
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-56936-4"} doi:10.1007/978-3-642-56936-4
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shlomo+Sternberg"}> Shlomo Sternberg
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Campbell Baker Hausdorff Formula
                %em Lie Algebras
                (2004) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://people.math.harvard.edu/~shlomo/docs/lie_algebras.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Sternberg-LieAlgebras.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#Milne17
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Milne"}> James Milne
                , p. 260 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Algebraic Groups – The theory of group schemes of finite type over a field
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/9781316711736"} doi:10.1017/9781316711736
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.jmilne.org/math/Books/iag.html"} webpage
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.jmilne.org/math/CourseNotes/iAG200.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Borcherds"}> Richard Borcherds
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Haiman"} Mark Haiman
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theo+Johnson-Freyd"} Theo Johnson-Freyd
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicolai+Reshetikhin"} Nicolai Reshetikhin
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vera+Serganova"} Vera Serganova
                %em Berkeley Lectures on Lie Groups and Quantum Groups
                (2020-2024) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://categorified.net/LieQuantumGroups.pdf"}> pdf
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Wikipedia:
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baker%E2%80%93Campbell%E2%80%93Hausdorff_formula"} Baker–Campbell–Hausdorff formula
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Terence+Tao"}> Terence Tao
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "https://terrytao.wordpress.com/2011/09/01/254a-notes-1-lie-groups-lie-algebras-and-the-baker-campbell-hausdorff-formula/"} 254A, Notes 1: Lie groups, Lie algebras, and the Baker-Campbell-Hausdorff formula
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Terence+Tao"}> Terence Tao
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "https://terrytao.wordpress.com/2011/06/21/the-c11-baker-campbell-hausdorff-formula"}
